data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/mission-report.md\", \"content\": \"# Mission report: greet, tested\\n\\n## Outcome\\ncampaign-met — all three stated criteria are satisfied.\\n\\n## Work performed\\n- Dispatched implementation to `dev` (dispatch d002): implement\\n  `src/greet.py` with `greet(name)` returning `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"`, and\\n  `tests/test_greet.py` covering a normal name and the empty string.\\n- `dev` replied with commit `69f4416` on branch\\n  `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`, built on the shared base\\n  `1053761f6a654e7ea58deb67a671a00d2e7fc8ac`.\\n\\n## Verification (independent of dev's self-report)\\n- Fetched dev's branch (`cs-campaign-member fetch dev`) into the\\n  orchestrator clone as `remotes/campaign/dev/subject`.\\n- Diffed it against base: only `src/greet.py` (2 lines) and\\n  `tests/test_greet.py` (19 lines) are added — no other files touched.\\n- Read both file contents directly from the commit tree via `git show`:\\n  - `src/greet.py`: `def greet(name): return f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"`\\n  - `tests/test_greet.py`: `unittest.TestCase` with `test_normal_name`\\n    (`greet(\\\"World\\\") == \\\"Hello, World!\\\"`) and `test_empty_string`\\n    (`greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`).\\n- Extracted the exact commit tree into a clean scratch directory\\n  (`git archive` of `remotes/campaign/dev/subject`) and ran\\n  `python3 -I -m unittest discover -s tests` myself, independent of dev's\\n  own machine. Result: `Ran 2 tests in 0.000s / OK`, exit code 0.\\n\\n## Judgment\\nAll three mission criteria confirmed met by direct inspection and\\nindependent test execution, not by trusting dev's report alone. Accepted\\nd002 from dev.\\n\\n## Orchestrator branch\\nNo code changes were made by the orchestrator (per role: judge, dispatch,\\ndo not write code). The orchestrator's own branch\\n(`cs-sandbox/<ORCHESTRATOR:1>.<GROUP:1>`) remains at base;\\nthe deliverable lives on `dev`'s branch\\n(`cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`, commit `69f4416`), which the\\nharness preserves independently as that teammate's own branch.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

